      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "IDEAL TIMING (1) continued his consistent form when fourth from a wider barrier here last week. Beaten just over a metre as runner-up here the last time he started on the pegs and should get every chance. FASTING (3) is hard to knock after winning three in a row at this circuit and distance. The good draw could see him add to that winning streak. PARTY CENTRAL NZ (9) has been a bit costly of late but hasn't been far away, chasing FASTING home at his last couple. With his A-game he is up to winning this. SAINT CRUSADER (10) is going well, winning two back at Newcastle before leading from a similar draw here last week and sticking on for second. With even luck he is a player again. MAURLEN BOY (6) must be respected after putting a string of top-four results together.",
